\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Each substep of $\Phi_h$ is canonical, preserving $\omega$. Symmetric
composition ensures $\Phi_{-h} = \Phi_h^{-1}$. Antisymmetry of
$\vec{F}_{\text{control}}$ guarantees that the reversed trajectory retraces the
forward path. Numerical errors are bounded by machine epsilon.
\end{proof}

